# Исходные фотографии квартиры — не публикуем
*.jpeg
*.jpg
*.JPEG
*.JPG
*.heic
*.HEIC

# ...except harness evidence frames, which are committed proof, not source
# photographs. On a case-insensitive filesystem the rules above swallow both
# `.jpg` and `.JPG`, so without this negation a harness frame written by
# CLAUDE.md's own screenshot recipe (`fetch('/save/shot.jpg', …)`) is silently
# unstageable: git reports no error, the evidence simply never lands. Keep this
# above the "Служебное" block so .DS_Store & co. stay ignored in here too.
!docs/superpowers/harnesses/**

# Vercel
.vercel

# Служебное
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
node_modules/
.playwright-mcp/

# Isolated worktrees and agent scratch space
.claude/worktrees/
.superpowers/

# Offscreen renders captured by tour/measure.js — build output, not source
tools/shots/

# Python bytecode from the measurement tools.
# `tools/**/__pycache__/` alone covers both `tools/__pycache__/` itself and
# nested directories such as `tools/checks/__pycache__/` — created by every
# run of stale_claims.py, which plan 4b added.
# ~~The general "no generic __pycache__ rule" row is still deferred~~
# **CLOSED 2026-08-23 by plan 5 task 5** with the generic rule below.
tools/**/__pycache__/

# The generic rule the deferred table asked for, added 2026-08-23 by plan 5
# task 5. It is NOT redundant with the line above: Python also lives under
# `docs/superpowers/harnesses/`, and line 15's `!docs/superpowers/harnesses/**`
# negation un-ignores everything there — including a `__pycache__/` a harness
# import would create. This rule sits AFTER that negation deliberately, because
# in gitignore the last matching rule wins. Placing it earlier would leave the
# harness directories uncovered, which is the shape of the hole this row
# existed to close: a stray `.pyc` was removed by hand once, "which worked
# because someone was paying attention, which is not a mechanism".
__pycache__/
